CAT = "ieqfaAml"; SEG = "AML"
Q = [
("Irish anti-money laundering obligations on financial firms come mainly from:",
 "The Criminal Justice Act 2010", ["The Consumer Credit Act 1995", "The Investment Intermediaries Act 1995 as amended", "The Insurance Act 1936 as amended"],
 "The Criminal Justice (Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing) Act 2010, as amended to implement later EU directives, sets the duties of designated persons."),
("Under the 2010 Act, a life assurance intermediary is a:",
 "Designated person", ["Prescribed reporting person", "Protected person", "Exempt person"],
 "Designated persons include credit and financial institutions, life insurers and intermediaries dealing in life assurance, and others named in the Act. They must apply customer due diligence and report suspicions."),
("Customer due diligence requires a firm to identify the customer and:",
 "Verify their identity reliably", ["Check their credit score with every bank", "Confirm their tax affairs with Revenue", "Visit the customer's home address in person"],
 "CDD means identifying the customer and any beneficial owner, verifying identity from documents or reliable independent sources, and understanding the purpose of the relationship."),
("For a company customer, a beneficial owner generally includes any individual who owns or controls more than:",
 "25% of it", ["5% of it", "10% of it", "50% or more of it"],
 "Under the EU directives and the 2010 Act, ownership or control of more than 25% of the shares or voting rights indicates a beneficial owner of a corporate body."),
("Which customer always calls for enhanced due diligence?",
 "A politically exposed person", ["A customer aged over 65", "A first-time house buyer", "A customer paying by direct debit"],
 "Business relationships with politically exposed persons, their family members and close associates require enhanced due diligence, including senior management approval and checks on the source of wealth and funds."),
("A politically exposed person includes a person who holds a prominent public function and also their:",
 "Family and close associates", ["Neighbours living on the same road", "Former school and college classmates", "Employer's other customers"],
 "The PEP rules extend to immediate family members and persons known to be close associates of the person holding the prominent public function."),
("An adviser suspects that a client's lump sum investment is the proceeds of crime. The suspicion must be reported to:",
 "FIU Ireland and Revenue", ["The client, so they can explain", "The FSPO and the client's own bank manager", "The Data Protection Commission"],
 "Suspicious transaction reports go to the Garda Financial Intelligence Unit (FIU Ireland) and to the Revenue Commissioners, as soon as practicable."),
("A client asks why his transaction is being delayed. His adviser has made a suspicious transaction report. The adviser must not:",
 "Reveal that a report was made", ["Keep a record of the client's call", "Tell her firm's compliance officer", "Follow her firm's AML procedures"],
 "Telling the client that a report has been made, or that an investigation is under way, in a way likely to prejudice it, is the offence of tipping off under the 2010 Act."),
("A designated person must keep customer due diligence records for at least how long after the business relationship ends?",
 "5 years", ["1 year", "3 years", "20 years"],
 "The 2010 Act requires CDD documents and transaction records to be kept for at least five years after the relationship ends or the transaction completes."),
("A firm cannot complete customer due diligence because the customer refuses to give documents. The firm should:",
 "Not proceed, and consider a report", ["Proceed and check documents later", "Accept a signed declaration of identity instead", "Ask a colleague to vouch for them"],
 "Where CDD cannot be completed, the designated person must not provide the service or carry out the transaction, and should consider whether a suspicious transaction report is needed."),
("The three classic stages of money laundering are:",
 "Placement, layering, integration", ["Saving, spending, investing", "Planning, buying, selling", "Lending, borrowing, and finally repaying"],
 "Criminal cash is placed into the system, layered through transactions to hide its origin, and integrated back into the economy as apparently legitimate funds."),
("A customer makes several deposits just below the level that would attract attention. This pattern is known as:",
 "Structuring", ["Churning", "Twisting", "Front running"],
 "Structuring, or smurfing, splits funds into smaller amounts to avoid triggering checks, and is a common red flag for money laundering."),
("Why can terrorist financing be harder to detect than money laundering?",
 "The funds may be legally earned", ["It always involves very large sums of cash", "It uses only cash, never banks", "It is not a criminal offence"],
 "Terrorist financing can use small amounts of legitimately earned money, so the focus is on where the funds are going rather than where they came from."),
("Under the 2010 Act, a designated person must assess the money laundering risks of its business and:",
 "Document it and keep it up to date", ["Publish it on its website for all clients to read", "Send it to every customer each year", "Have it approved by each client"],
 "Designated persons must carry out and document a business risk assessment, keep it up to date and use it to set their policies, controls and the level of due diligence applied."),
("A firm finds that a new client's name matches a person on an EU financial sanctions list. The firm must:",
 "Freeze the funds and report it", ["Accept the money but tell no one", "Return the funds with interest", "Ask the client to change the name"],
 "EU restrictive measures require funds of listed persons to be frozen and not made available to them, with the match reported to the Central Bank, the competent authority for financial sanctions."),
("A designated person must make sure its staff:",
 "Are trained to spot suspicious activity", ["Hold a qualification in criminal law", "Interview every customer in person", "Report all cash payments to the Gardaí every week"],
 "The 2010 Act requires designated persons to give staff ongoing training on the law and on recognising and handling transactions that may involve money laundering or terrorist financing."),
]
